"span",{className:"highlight-text",children:"Sliding Window Attention"})," ","(SWA). Our extensive empirical results show that SWA is simple, efficient, and easy to use, delivering better overall performance than Linear Attention across general tasks, long-context payload, and reasoning. It also provides a fixed-size KV cache, making it easy to integrate with existing training and inference infrastructure. We redefined parallel decoding to achieve extremely high output token throughput: by introducing"," ",(0,i.jsx)("span",{className:"highlight-text",children:"Multi-Token Prediction"})," (MTP) training, we boost the base model's capabilities, and during inference we validate MTP tokens in parallel."]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-container",children:[(0,i.jsx)("h3",{className:"chart-title",children:"Multi-Token Prediction"}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-split",children:[(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-panel-left",children:[(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-input-label-row",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-label",children:"verify"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-hint",children:"← draft from previous MTP"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-row mtp-row-4",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-white",children:"token i"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft",children:"token i+1"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft",children:"token i+2"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft",children:"token i+3"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-arrows mtp-arrows-4",children:[(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"})]}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-model",children:"Language Model (verify)"}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-arrows mtp-arrows-4",children:[(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-row mtp-row-4",children:[(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-result",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-accept",children:"token i+1"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-status mtp-status-accept",children:"accept"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-result",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-accept",children:"token i+2"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-status mtp-status-accept",children:"accept"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-result",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-blue",children:"token i+3"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-status mtp-status-regenerate",children:"reject"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-result",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-abandon",children:"token i+4"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-status mtp-status-abandon",children:"abandoned"})]})]})]}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-divider"}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-panel-right",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-label",children:"generate"}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-row mtp-row-3",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-blue",children:"token i+3"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft-dashed",children:"token i+4"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft-dashed",children:"token i+5"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-arrows mtp-arrows-3",children:[(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-row mtp-row-3",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-model mtp-model-mtp mtp-model-small",children:"MTP 1"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-model mtp-model-mtp mtp-model-small",children:"MTP 2"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-model mtp-model-mtp mtp-model-small",children:"MTP 3"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-arrows mtp-arrows-3",children:[(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"}),(0,i.jsx)("span",{children:"↓"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("div",{className:"mtp-row mtp-row-3",children:[(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft",children:"token i+4"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft",children:"token i+5"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-token mtp-token-draft",children:"token i+6"})]}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"mtp-draft-label",children:"drafts"})]})]})]}),(0,i.jsx)("p",{children:"MiMo-V2-Flash leverages MTP as a native draft model for self-speculative decoding, delivering real deployment speedups. LLM decoding is inherently memory-bound due to low arithmetic intensity. Batch-level parallelism is commonly used to increase FFN arithmetic intensity but does not benefit attention computation, as each request maintains its own KV cache. In contrast, MTP lifts the arithmetic intensity of both FFN and attention by generating multiple draft tokens, which the main model then verifies in parallel. This approach enables token-level parallelism without increasing KV cache I/O. In MiMo-V2-Flash, the MTP block is deliberately kept lightweight to prevent it from becoming a new inference bottleneck. It uses a dense FFN (not MoE) to limit parameter count and SWA (instead of GA) to reduce KV cache and attention computation costs. Despite this lean design, the MTP module achieves a high acceptance rate. In our measurements with a 3-layer MTP, it attains an accepted length of 2.8–3.6 tokens and an effective speedup of 2.0–2.6\xd7."})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("section",{className:"section",children:[(0,i.jsx)("h2",{children:"MOPD: A New Post-Training Paradigm"}),(0,i.jsxs)("p",{children:["During the post-training phase, to efficiently scale reinforcement learning (RL) computation and enhance the model's reasoning and agentic capabilities, we propose the"," ",(0,i.jsx)("span",{className:"highlight-text",children:"Multi-Teacher Online Policy Distillation"})," ","(MOPD) paradigm. At its core lies an efficient on-policy learning mechanism: after obtaining domain-specific expert teachers via SFT/RL, the student model samples (rollouts) from its own policy distribution and optimizes using dense, token-level rewards provided by multiple teachers."]}),(0,i.jsx)("p",{children:"MOPD training is stable and remarkably efficient—requiring less than 1/50 of the computational resources of traditional SFT+RL pipelines to match the peak performance of teacher models."}),(0,i.jsx)("p",{children:'Furthermore, MOPD employs a decoupled design that supports flexible integration of new teachers and ORMs, and naturally enables a "teach and learn" closed-loop iteration: distilled student models can evolve into stronger teachers, achieving continuous self-improvement of capabilities.'}),(0,i.jsxs)("figure",{className:"mopd-figure",children:[(0,i.jsx)("img",{src:"/mimo-v2-flash/assets/post-training.svg",alt:"MOPD Architecture Diagram"}),(0,i.jsx)("figcaption",{children:"Post-Training Pipeline"})]})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("section",{className:"section evaluation-section",children:[(0,i.jsx)("h2",{children:"Evaluation"}),(0,i.jsx)("p",{children:"We evaluate MiMo-V2-Flash across a broad suite of benchmarks:"}),(0,i.jsx)("div",{className:"evaluation-table-container",children:(0,i.jsxs)("table",{className:"evaluation-table",id:"evaluation-table",children:[(0,i.jsxs)("thead",{children:[(0,i.jsxs)("tr",{className:"header-row",children:[(0,i.jsx)("th",{rowSpan:2,className:"benchmark-col",children:"Benchmark"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col mimo-col",children:"MiMo-V2"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Kimi-K2"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"DeepSeek-V3.2"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Gemini-3.0"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Claude"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"GPT-5"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("tr",{className:"subheader-row",children:[(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col mimo-col",children:"Flash"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Thinking"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Thinking"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Pro"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"Sonnet 4.5"}),(0,i.jsx)("th",{className:"model-col",children:"High"})]})]}),(0,i.jsx)("tbody",{id:"evaluation-tbody"})]})}),(0,i.jsx)("p",{children:"MiMo-V2-Flash achieves performance comparable to K2 Thinking and DeepSeek V3.2 Thinking on most reasoning benchmarks, while maintaining competitive general writing capabilities for high-quality open-ended responses. In long-context evaluations, our model surpasses K2 Thinking, a significantly larger full global attention LLM, highlighting the strong long-context capabilities of our hybrid SWA architecture."}),(0,i.jsx)("p",{children:"On agentic tasks, MiMo-V2-Flash scores 73.4% on SWE-Bench Verified, outperforming all open-source competitors and approaching the performance of GPT-5-High. On SWE-Bench Multilingual, the model resolves 71.7% of issues, establishing it as the most capable open-source LLM for software engineering. For general tool-use on τ\xb2-Bench, it achieves category scores of 95.3 (Telecom), 79.5 (Retail), 66.0 (Airline). Terminal Bench results also show a competitive score. For search agent evaluation, MiMo-V2-Flash scores 45.4 on BrowseComp, further boosted to 58.3 with context management."})]}),(0,i.jsxs)("section",{className:"section",children:[(0,i.jsx)("h2",{children:"Open-source"}),(0,i.jsxs)("p",{children:["As usual, we are open-sourcing everything. Read our"," ",(0,i.jsx)("a",{href:"https://github.com/XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2-Flash/blob/main/paper.pdf",target:"_blank",children:"technical report"})," ","for full model details."]}),(0,i.jsxs)("p",{children:["Model weights, including MiMo-V2-Flash-Base, are available on"," ",(0,i.jsx)("a",{href:"https://huggingface.co/xiaomimimo/MiMo-V2-Flash",target:"_blank",children:"Hugging Face"})," ","under the MIT license."]}),(0,i.jsxs)("p",{children:["On Day 0, we contributed all inference code to"," ",(0,i.jsx